  "flags": [
    {
      "page": 5,
      "what": "The three skill tables' ticks are glyphs the text layer drops: they were read from p5's image. Each house is a variant, holding its own table. Fierezza (the first, so the fighters' own) - Commander: all five lists; Sergeant: Combat, Shooting, Speed; Adjutant: Combat, Academic, Speed. Halcon - Commander: all five; Sergeant: Combat, Shooting, Strength; Adjutant: Shooting, Academic, Speed. Baluardo - Commander: all five; Sergeant: Combat, Strength, Speed; Adjutant: Academic, Strength, Speed. There is no Special column, so the warband has no skill group."
    },
    {
      "page": 3,
      "what": "The Heroes list marks Rapier and Sword breaker House Fierezza only, Crossbow pistol and Longbow House Halcon only, and Plate armour and Pavise House Baluardo only: each of the six lines is its house's variant line on the one Heroes list."
    },
    {
      "page": 2,
      "what": "Merchantry (the Commander starts with Haggle) is printed in House Halcon's column, below Sharp Aim; Battle Seasoned and Armour are House Baluardo's. The reading order runs the two columns together."
    },
    {
      "page": 5,
      "what": "The Pike's entry (10 gc, Rare 8, Two-handed and Strike first with +1 Initiative in the first turn) is read as our Pike, with a House Guard price row at 10 gc Rare 8. Ours carries those same two rules (Border Town Burning). It was read as Pike (Tileans), the Lustria pike that reaches 3\", until William discontinued that one (11 Nov 2026: \"the tilean one got discontinued\") and this became the only pike."
    },
    {
      "page": 5,
      "what": "Plate armour is 55 gc on the Heroes list and 70 gc Rare 7 in its own entry: the list price is the starting price and the entry's is the trading price (William, 6 Nov 2026)."
    },
    {
      "page": 2,
      "what": "Martial Finesse (Fierezza), Merchantry (Halcon) and Battle Seasoned (Baluardo) each only name a skill the Commander starts with (Web of Steel, Haggle, Battle Tongue), so he is given it by his variant and none stays a rule (William, 7 Nov 2026)."
    },
    {
      "page": 2,
      "what": "A House Guard needs at least 3 models: our templates hold no minimum, so it is not imported."
    },
    {
      "page": 4,
      "what": "No group sizes are printed for the Guards, Pikemen or Warhounds."
    }
  ]
}
